the deepening crisis over ukraine new  details are emerging about how the  american government believes that russia  could justify a potential invasion with  large russian military forces already  deployed near ukraine american officials  say moscow could use a fabricated video  of a fake ukrainian attack as a pretext  to their own real invasion russia denies  it has any plans for a so-called false  flag operation however holly williams is  in ukraine for us as she's been for days  now holly good morning  good morning a senior u.s administration  official told cbs news russia may have  already recruited people to fake a  deadly attack but the truth is the u.s  has been warning of phony incidents set  up by russia for weeks  we believe that russia would produce a  very graphic propaganda video  which would include corpses  and actors that would be depicting  mourners  and images of destroyed locations with  around 100 000 russian troops masked on  ukraine's border  the us is warning that moscow could  stage a violent incident and blame  ukrainian forces as a pretext for moving  in  the u.s government says a fake attack  could involve military equipment  purported to be supplied by the west and  explosions and the pretend victims could  be in russia or russian-speaking people  here in ukraine  the u.s has not provided any supporting  evidence but claims by going public it's  trying to dissuade russia before it acts  the u.s has warned of similar plots  before and of russian disinformation  this is straight out of the russian  playbook  and they're not fooling us  one example is a russian state tv report  in 2014 that a three-year-old child was  crucified by ukrainian forces now widely  thought to be a fabrication  maria sahidak works for ukraine's  government calling out russian  propaganda they want to to confuse  people and to build this  fake reality that doesn't exist  russia's president vladimir putin is in  beijing today for the olympics opening  ceremony and he's been meeting with  china's leader xi jinping china and  russia have grown much closer in recent  years and more at odds with the us if  vladimir putin did decide to attack  ukraine and remember russia claims it  has no plans to invade china's support  could be crucial the u.s has threatened  to respond with sanctions and china with  its giant economy could potentially  offset the impact of those sanctions  whether they target banks or supply  chains gail  thank you holly the world is certainly  watching holly williams reporting from  ukraine
 

